//-------------Time-complexity--------------------------------

/*
Definition: Time complexity is a measure of how an algorithm's runtime grows
with respect to the input size.
*/

// basically,Time-complexity depends on input size not time-taken by machine to run the code

/*
Three rules:
1.always use worst-case
2.avoid constant terms(ex:O(2n)->O(n))
3.avoid lower values(ex:O(n+1)->O(n))
*/

/*
there are mainly three cases:
1.best-case:when code excute in first case
2.worst-case:when code runs untill last condition
3.average- case:case between worst and best case
*/

/*Example:Finding max element in array:
best-case:we found max at first element  of array
worst-case:we found at last
average-case:we found in between
*/

/*
there are mainly 3rd ways to define Time-Complexity:
1.big-O notation: worst-case[upper bound];
2.theta : average-case
3.Omega : best-case[lower bound]
*/

//---------------Space-complexity-----------------------------------------------

/*
adition of auxiliary space and the input space.
here auxiliary = space we take to solve problem
input = space we use to take input
it is defined by big-O notations
example: input a;
         input b;[input space O(1)]
         c = a+b;[auxiliary space O(1)]
*/

/*
notes: 1.Don't manipulate given data[example : b = a+b]
         2.On online server when we run our code server executes roughly 10^8
         operations in 1 sec
         time limit n sec = n*10^8 operations

*/


// ============ PRACTICE QUESTIONS ============

/* 
QUESTION 1: Sequential Loops (Linear Time)
Code:
    for(int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        cout << i;
    }
    for(int j = 0; j < n; j++) {
        cout << j;
    }

ANSWER:
    Time Complexity: O(n)
    - First loop: O(n) iterations
    - Second loop: O(n) iterations
    - Total: O(n) + O(n) = O(2n) → O(n) [ignore constants]
    
    Space Complexity: O(1)
    - Only using loop variables (constant space)
*/

/* 
QUESTION 2: Nested Loops (Quadratic Time)
Code:
    for(int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        for(int j = 0; j < n; j++) {
            cout << i*j;
        }
    }

ANSWER:
    Time Complexity: O(n²)
    - Outer loop: n iterations
    - Inner loop: n iterations (for each outer iteration)
    - Total: n² = O(n²)
    
    Space Complexity: O(1)
    - No auxiliary data structures used
*/

